/// known-gap: interp has no tick() block or phase: blocks; the interpreter is being retired
/// A `tick()` block runs the phases it names, in order, and the tick ends
/// where the block does: what is in no phase runs then, and the tick count
/// moves once. A phase line can repeat (`repeat`). `every N ticks` in a
/// phase counts the tick it is part of. A bare `tick()` runs only what is
/// in no phase. A field may still be named `phase`.
<>Land |
    food: 0
    phase: 1
    log: ..
    phase: grow
        every 1 tick
            @food |= @food + 2
            @log |= "{@log}g"
        xx
        every 2 ticks
            @log |= "{@log}2"
        xx
    xx
    phase: eat
        decision feast
            targets: Land where target >> food > 3
            score => target >> food
        xx
        judge
            feast: self.eat_from(feast >> target)
        xx
    xx
    every 1 tick
        @log |= "{@log}e"
    xx
    act eat_from(t)
        t >> food |= t >> food - 3
        @log |= "{@log}f"
    xx
xx
a <> Land | food: 0
b <> Land | food: 1
repeat 3
    tick()
        grow
        eat
    xx
    say("{a >> food} {b >> food} {a >> log} {b >> log} {:metrics(){"ticks"}}")
xx
tick()
    repeat 2
        grow
    xx
xx
say("{a >> food} {b >> food} {a >> log} {:metrics(){"ticks"}}")
tick()
say("{a >> food} {a >> log} {:metrics(){"ticks"}} {a >> phase}")
